WEBVTT

00:11.011 --> 00:13.013
[rock music playing]

00:43.043 --> 00:46.172
CHAPTER 34:
I'M THEIR HOMEROOM TEACHER

00:46.255 --> 00:50.259
[chuckling] The-The States?
Sounds like a nice plan.

00:50.342 --> 00:54.555
Fair enough, though. I heard you got
many offers from many places.

00:54.638 --> 00:59.351
So then, are you going to go study
at a place like Harvard or MIT?

00:59.435 --> 01:01.604
Or are you going to be a professor there?

01:01.687 --> 01:04.565
[chuckles] Uh…

01:04.648 --> 01:08.694
How long does something like that
usually take? A semester?

01:09.487 --> 01:11.238
Is it a year? I mean…

01:11.822 --> 01:13.365
I mean… [sighs]

01:15.367 --> 01:17.745
If it's something that will take long,

01:18.662 --> 01:23.250
I'm wondering if I won't get to see you
in my senior year.

01:25.795 --> 01:27.004
[sighs]

01:30.966 --> 01:32.843
It's late. Go home.

01:35.471 --> 01:36.514
Gosh.

01:37.014 --> 01:38.098
Get home safely, okay?

01:48.275 --> 01:50.569
So when will you be leaving?

01:51.278 --> 01:53.280
[forlorn music playing]

01:58.494 --> 01:59.495
[sighs]

01:59.578 --> 02:02.790
What do you think
about your friend's offer? Na Deul-i's?

02:03.374 --> 02:04.375
[sighs]

02:05.084 --> 02:07.211
So when you have a chance
to go to the States

02:07.294 --> 02:08.420
and do the research you wanna do…

02:09.046 --> 02:10.047
[groans]

02:11.006 --> 02:12.758
[inhales sharply, sighs]

02:15.261 --> 02:18.973
I wonder, why does he have to go
with that lady though?

02:20.307 --> 02:24.186
I guess she really is his girlfriend.

02:25.980 --> 02:27.648
[clicks tongue, sighs]

02:27.731 --> 02:30.150
Yeah, he's human after all.

02:30.234 --> 02:31.986
Of course he'd have a love life.

02:33.445 --> 02:35.447
[sighs]

02:35.531 --> 02:37.449
They'll do research together

02:38.409 --> 02:39.994
in the States.

02:40.703 --> 02:42.162
Just the two of them.

02:43.998 --> 02:45.374
Good for them.

02:47.042 --> 02:48.627
[sighs]

02:50.170 --> 02:51.255
Hold on a second.

02:51.338 --> 02:53.173
If I hadn't found that out today,

02:53.257 --> 02:55.217
when was he going to let us know?

02:56.218 --> 02:57.344
At the end of the year?

02:57.428 --> 03:00.014
Was he going to be like,
"Hey, I'm off to the States."

03:01.640 --> 03:02.808
[sighs]

03:04.768 --> 03:05.769
Whatever.

03:07.146 --> 03:09.231
He doesn't have to tell us anyway.

03:10.190 --> 03:14.194
Whether he leaves or he stays,
that's his life.

03:15.029 --> 03:17.781
[sighs] And I'm just one
of his many students.

03:28.626 --> 03:30.628
EPISODE 11

03:30.711 --> 03:32.046
[indistinct chattering]

03:35.966 --> 03:37.301
[students] Hello.

03:37.384 --> 03:38.636
[student] Hey, hi.

03:43.682 --> 03:45.225
Are only Choi Ji-a and Jenny missing?

03:45.976 --> 03:47.311
-[students] Yes.
-Yes.

03:47.394 --> 03:49.563
Applications
for the career experience program

03:49.647 --> 03:51.440
are open until the end of this week.

03:51.941 --> 03:53.609
Check the group chat
for the announcements,

03:53.692 --> 03:56.278
and if you're interested,
submit an application from to Eun Ha-su.

03:56.362 --> 03:57.780
[students] Okay.

03:57.863 --> 03:59.823
-Make sure you bring them to me.
-[Ha-su] Okay.

04:00.908 --> 04:03.869
-That's all.
-[students] Thank you.

04:07.122 --> 04:10.167
Hey, Choi Ji-a's isn't here again.
What now?

04:10.250 --> 04:12.795
-What if you get more demerits now?
-[sighs]

04:12.878 --> 04:14.880
Do you think something happened to her?

04:16.173 --> 04:18.926
-[Yeong-jae] Like what?
-Ugh, I don't know.

04:21.887 --> 04:22.972
[sighs]

04:35.818 --> 04:37.361
How may I help you?

04:37.444 --> 04:38.445
Hello, ma'am.

04:38.529 --> 04:40.155
My name is Yeo Eui-ju,

04:40.239 --> 04:41.949
-and I'm Ji-a's classmate.
-Oh.

04:42.032 --> 04:46.328
She wasn't in school and I was wondering
if something happened to her.

04:46.412 --> 04:48.080
Well, she isn't here right now.

04:48.580 --> 04:49.999
She's probably working.

04:50.958 --> 04:52.334
Ah.

04:52.418 --> 04:54.586
Do you know where she works by any chance?

04:54.670 --> 04:56.839
Where was it? [puffs air] Uh…

04:56.922 --> 04:59.091
I heard it was a hamburger place.

04:59.174 --> 05:01.093
The one at the intersection
near the hospital.

05:01.176 --> 05:03.387
Ah. Ah, I see.

05:04.054 --> 05:05.973
-Thank you so much.
-Thank you for coming by

05:06.056 --> 05:07.433
to see if she's okay.

05:08.308 --> 05:09.518
Goodbye now.

05:12.187 --> 05:14.773
[door opens, closes]

05:15.482 --> 05:16.483
Oh.

05:16.567 --> 05:17.776
Mr. Ga.

05:19.653 --> 05:21.363
Ji-a isn't here right now.

05:21.447 --> 05:22.823
She's out working.

05:24.158 --> 05:25.617
How did you get here?

05:27.119 --> 05:31.040
Last year I saw her write down her address
on a piece of paper.

05:32.666 --> 05:34.209
Why don't you go home? I'll look for her.

05:36.879 --> 05:38.088
No.

05:39.089 --> 05:41.050
I'm sick of doing demerit duty,

05:41.133 --> 05:42.760
and I have to see Ji-a today.

05:45.387 --> 05:46.847
But… [sighs]

05:54.521 --> 05:56.065
-[worker] Ji-a?
-Yes.

05:56.148 --> 05:58.233
-She doesn't work here anymore.
-Huh?

05:58.776 --> 05:59.943
Since when?

06:00.027 --> 06:01.945
Uh, two weeks ago.

06:02.029 --> 06:03.530
No, no, no. Three weeks ago.

06:03.614 --> 06:07.618
Oh, uh, do you by any chance know
where she might be right now?

06:08.619 --> 06:09.828
A ribs restaurant.

06:09.912 --> 06:12.456
I heard she works there
because they pay her a lot more.

06:12.539 --> 06:14.124
-Do you know the name?
-I don't.

06:14.208 --> 06:15.751
I didn't ask.

06:17.753 --> 06:19.463
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

06:22.966 --> 06:24.218
[sighs]

06:25.594 --> 06:27.596
I'll go this way,
and you can try that way.

06:27.679 --> 06:29.223
-Let me know if you find her.
-Okay.

06:30.349 --> 06:32.351
[funky pop music playing]

06:37.564 --> 06:39.566
[no audible dialogue]

07:02.923 --> 07:04.091
Oh…

07:05.801 --> 07:09.179
Dang. What… What's wrong with that guy?

07:10.305 --> 07:11.390
Come on now.

07:13.267 --> 07:14.476
What's the matter with you?

07:14.560 --> 07:15.811
Are you nuts?

07:15.894 --> 07:18.313
Hey, you shouldn't drink
just because they offer it to you.

07:18.397 --> 07:19.815
Do they even know you're a high schooler?

07:20.774 --> 07:22.234
They tip me for it.

07:22.317 --> 07:23.443
Wouldn't you do the same?

07:24.862 --> 07:26.822
Hey, come on. Even then…

07:26.905 --> 07:28.157
Ji-a?

07:28.824 --> 07:29.908
Ji-a.

07:29.992 --> 07:33.453
Yeah, we got her. It's her. [laughing]

07:33.537 --> 07:35.164
Today's the day, isn't it?

07:35.247 --> 07:36.498
Right?

07:37.457 --> 07:39.585
I haven't gotten paid yet, though.

07:39.668 --> 07:40.961
-Next time--
-"Next time"?

07:41.044 --> 07:42.379
[laughs]

07:42.462 --> 07:44.965
You told us
the exact same thing last time.

07:45.799 --> 07:47.593
We're not a charity group.

07:47.676 --> 07:49.386
Come on, what's wrong with you?

07:49.469 --> 07:51.763
We need to put food
on the table, all right?

07:51.847 --> 07:53.599
I really don't have money.

07:53.682 --> 07:56.393
-If you don't, then make some, huh?
-Damn.

07:56.476 --> 07:57.853
There's lots of places to work.

07:57.936 --> 08:03.734
Convenience stores, karaokes,
burger joints, bars. No?

08:04.401 --> 08:05.903
The way I see it, dear,

08:06.653 --> 08:10.407
-you're going to find the money no matter…
-Whoa, what are you doing? Stop it.

08:10.490 --> 08:12.117
Are you her friend?

08:12.201 --> 08:13.577
Well, are you?

08:13.660 --> 08:15.370
What? You think we're gonna
do something to her?

08:15.454 --> 08:16.496
We're not bad guys.

08:16.580 --> 08:18.457
And if you're that worried,

08:18.540 --> 08:20.751
you can pay off
your friend's debts for her.

08:20.834 --> 08:22.711
-[laughs]
-Do you have any money, friend?

08:23.503 --> 08:24.880
-Huh?
-Wait, we're scaring her.

08:24.963 --> 08:26.131
Stop it, stop it.

08:26.215 --> 08:29.468
Well then,
how much can you pay us back today?

08:30.427 --> 08:32.804
I swear, I have no money.

08:32.888 --> 08:35.891
-Damn it, are you trying to mess with me?
-What are you doing?

08:35.974 --> 08:38.352
-Stop it! Let go of her!
-You shouldn't do this!

08:38.435 --> 08:41.104
Huh? What the… Damn.

08:41.897 --> 08:42.898
-Ow.
-What the heck?

08:42.981 --> 08:44.233
Who the hell are you?

08:44.900 --> 08:45.901
Well?

08:46.485 --> 08:47.986
I'm their homeroom teacher.

08:49.154 --> 08:50.322
Ah.

08:50.405 --> 08:52.741
-You scared me.
-Damn, you're a teacher, huh?

08:53.325 --> 08:54.493
This is actually better.

08:54.576 --> 08:57.246
Why don't you just pay off her debt
on her behalf then?

08:57.329 --> 08:59.206
You're the ones who did this
to her too, didn't you?

09:00.249 --> 09:01.917
[thug 2] We wouldn't know
anything about that.

09:02.626 --> 09:04.378
-Hey, teach.
-[groans]

09:04.461 --> 09:07.923
This girl right here
borrowed money from us, all right?

09:08.006 --> 09:10.884
Doesn't school teach its students
to pay back what they borrow these days?

09:10.968 --> 09:12.010
[thug 1] Exactly.

09:15.597 --> 09:16.640
How much did she borrow?

09:16.723 --> 09:19.142
How much, you ask? Ha.

09:19.226 --> 09:21.561
It was about 340.

09:22.354 --> 09:25.691
But now, 1,700.

09:27.609 --> 09:28.860
Is that all she has to pay?

09:28.944 --> 09:31.571
-[loan sharks laugh]
-Mr. Ga!

09:31.655 --> 09:35.325
That's right.
Whoa, you're pretty cool, teach, hmm?

09:35.409 --> 09:37.077
-[thug 2] Awesome.
-[thug 1] That's right.

09:37.160 --> 09:39.204
-All right then, here.
-Yeah.

09:39.288 --> 09:40.956
Wire the money to this account.

09:41.039 --> 09:42.958
Can you see it? Okay?

09:43.041 --> 09:45.085
-[phone beeps]
-I just did.

09:45.168 --> 09:46.378
-[thug 1] Oh, you did?
-[thug 2] Did he?

09:46.461 --> 09:47.921
-[thug 1] Great. Uh-huh.
-[thug 2] Great.

09:49.339 --> 09:51.341
Say she's debt free
while I take a video of you.

09:53.760 --> 09:55.679
-On November 10th…
-Yeah.

09:55.762 --> 10:00.142
-…we received $1700 from Choi Ji-a.
-We did.

10:00.225 --> 10:04.146
Since she's debt free,
we will never contact Choi Ji-a again.

10:04.646 --> 10:06.273
-Happy now?
-Happy?

10:06.356 --> 10:07.274
[phone beeps]

10:07.357 --> 10:09.067
Delete her number from your phones now.

10:09.151 --> 10:12.946
-Okay. Choi Ji-a. "Delete number." There.
-Here.

10:13.030 --> 10:14.031
DELETE NUMBER

10:14.114 --> 10:15.532
-[thug 2] Okay?
-[thug 1] Happy now?

10:15.615 --> 10:17.659
Stay away from her for good.

10:17.743 --> 10:19.578
-[chuckles] Yes, sir.
-Got it.

10:20.537 --> 10:22.039
It was an honor to meet you today.

10:22.122 --> 10:23.915
-And if you ever need to take out a loan…
-Yeah.

10:23.999 --> 10:25.208
…call us at this number here.

10:25.876 --> 10:27.169
All right?

10:27.252 --> 10:29.421
-The number's on the business card, okay?
-That's right.

10:30.339 --> 10:32.382
-We'll be waiting.
-We'll give you special treatment.

10:32.466 --> 10:34.134
-Bye-bye.
-We're leaving, Ji-a.

10:34.217 --> 10:35.635
Bye-bye.

10:43.310 --> 10:44.519
Mr. Ga,

10:45.979 --> 10:47.689
I'll pay you back for sure.

10:47.773 --> 10:50.400
I mean it. Even if it takes a long time.

10:50.484 --> 10:52.110
I'll make sure to pay you back.

10:53.362 --> 10:54.738
Forget it.

10:54.821 --> 10:57.574
You just have to stop skipping school,
and do better.

10:59.284 --> 11:00.285
But still…

11:00.369 --> 11:03.914
If you wanna pay me back,
then why don't you help a kid in need?

11:04.664 --> 11:06.625
Later, when you grow up or something.

11:12.422 --> 11:14.091
-What are you doing?
-Huh?

11:16.218 --> 11:17.219
Well…

11:17.302 --> 11:19.763
it'd be good to get a picture
of the evidence.

11:21.223 --> 11:23.475
You seriously love taking pictures
and videos.

11:24.601 --> 11:25.811
Let's go.

11:28.271 --> 11:29.981
-Come on.
-Okay.

11:35.570 --> 11:38.865
Why didn't you report them
after all this time?

11:39.616 --> 11:42.577
One of the shelter kids
was in a similar situation.

11:43.787 --> 11:46.832
She borrowed money from loan sharks
and got harassed for it.

11:47.791 --> 11:49.835
She reported them to the police,

11:49.918 --> 11:52.254
but they raided the shelter
and made a big scene.

11:53.797 --> 11:55.632
So she had to move out

11:55.715 --> 11:58.051
for causing harm
to the other shelter kids.

11:58.635 --> 11:59.636
Oh.

12:00.262 --> 12:01.555
I see now.

12:02.556 --> 12:05.684
So, can you work a bit less from now on?

12:08.145 --> 12:09.521
I can't.

12:09.604 --> 12:10.856
I need the money.

12:11.815 --> 12:14.067
I have to move out of the shelter
next year,

12:14.693 --> 12:19.406
so I need to save at least $3000
for a deposit and rent

12:19.489 --> 12:20.782
just to get by.

12:22.325 --> 12:23.618
Oh.

12:23.702 --> 12:24.911
I see.

12:27.080 --> 12:28.623
[sighs]

12:28.707 --> 12:31.084
CLOUD YOUTH SHELTER

12:37.007 --> 12:38.341
Thank you very much.

12:39.134 --> 12:40.594
Mmm.

12:41.678 --> 12:42.679
Get home safe.

12:43.472 --> 12:45.432
Mmm. I'll see you at school.

12:51.354 --> 12:52.481
[exhales sharply]

13:00.197 --> 13:02.574
-Let's go.
-Okay.

13:04.951 --> 13:07.662
Ji-a told me she couldn't report them

13:07.746 --> 13:10.874
because they could go to the shelter
and make a big scene.

13:10.957 --> 13:13.084
[sighs]

13:13.168 --> 13:14.586
She was afraid.

13:16.213 --> 13:19.424
I didn't think you'd come
all the way here for her.

13:20.217 --> 13:23.637
Other teachers don't even bother
whether she comes to school or not.

13:25.514 --> 13:28.350
I bet you didn't come all the way here
because of demerits.

13:28.433 --> 13:30.018
You were worried about her.

13:34.189 --> 13:35.273
I'm proud of you.

13:38.735 --> 13:39.986
[chuckles]

13:41.279 --> 13:44.199
Anyway, if you decide to go to the States,

13:44.282 --> 13:48.453
is it because, over there,
you can do what you really want?

13:50.330 --> 13:51.581
Well, you know,

13:52.290 --> 13:54.334
just like I love writing novels,

13:54.417 --> 13:56.545
you may have something
you really love too.

13:57.587 --> 13:59.256
Something…

13:59.339 --> 14:02.759
Something that you just can't live
without doing at all.

14:02.842 --> 14:05.345
I'm wondering
if that's why you would leave.

14:08.682 --> 14:10.308
Yes, maybe that's true.

14:11.726 --> 14:16.356
But whatever it is, my priority right now
is teaching you girls

14:16.439 --> 14:17.649
while looking after you

14:18.441 --> 14:19.985
and keeping an eye on all of you.

14:21.945 --> 14:23.196
There is nothing else.

14:29.411 --> 14:31.705
[peaceful music playing]

15:03.945 --> 15:04.988
[exhales sharply]

15:11.620 --> 15:12.704
[sighs]

15:13.580 --> 15:15.749
[tender music playing]

15:27.177 --> 15:30.972
CHAPTER 35:
WE'LL HELP LIKE YOU'RE FAMILY

15:33.266 --> 15:35.935
[students chattering]

15:44.486 --> 15:46.029
Girls, what's up?

15:46.112 --> 15:47.989
-[student] Jenny!
-I'm back.

15:48.073 --> 15:49.157
[students clamoring]

15:49.240 --> 15:52.952
It's a present for you guys. Enjoy.

15:53.036 --> 15:56.039
-Jenny! Hi!
-Jenny! I missed you so much.

15:56.122 --> 15:58.166
-I'm back. Here you go.
-Hurry, get over here.

15:58.249 --> 15:59.918
[gasps] Thank you.

16:00.001 --> 16:03.296
In Yeonnam, I had to wait in line
for an hour and a half

16:03.380 --> 16:04.464
just to get these cookies.

16:04.547 --> 16:07.175
-That looks so good.
-[chuckling]

16:07.258 --> 16:08.218
Thank you.

16:12.389 --> 16:14.182
-Thanks.
-[gasps]

16:15.850 --> 16:17.143
You're welcome.

16:18.144 --> 16:19.145
[exclaims]

16:19.229 --> 16:20.939
[Dan-ji] Jenny, these are to die for.

16:21.022 --> 16:22.607
-I know! Yum!
-Mm-hmm.

16:22.691 --> 16:24.401
Jenny, I saw you posted so many stories.

16:24.484 --> 16:26.528
They just kept popping up
one after the other.

16:26.611 --> 16:28.238
Went to a lot of places.

16:28.321 --> 16:30.782
From super early in the morning
to late at night.

16:30.865 --> 16:33.118
Aw. My feet hurt so much.

16:33.201 --> 16:35.662
Oh, I got blisters too. Want to see them?

16:35.745 --> 16:37.914
-Oh, um, I don't think that's necessary.
-Uh, no thanks.

16:37.997 --> 16:39.874
-Really.
-Mm-hmm.

16:39.958 --> 16:41.084
[clicks tongue] Your loss.

16:42.585 --> 16:45.171
-Go-ya, come eat with us.
-Mmm. [chuckles]

16:45.255 --> 16:47.090
-Thanks. I'm okay.
-[Jenny] Have some.

16:47.173 --> 16:49.300
-What is it?
-[chuckling nervously]

16:49.384 --> 16:50.969
-Hey, why…
-Jenny.

16:51.052 --> 16:53.221
-[Jenny] She doesn't want it?
-[Dan-ji] Jenny. Uh…

16:53.304 --> 16:55.098
We'll talk in the group chat, okay?

16:55.181 --> 16:57.392
Oh, give us some updates
on where to go in Seoul, okay?

16:57.475 --> 17:00.687
-Like the Han River and…
-Of course.

17:00.770 --> 17:02.397
Oh, oh. Sit down.

17:02.480 --> 17:04.274
[students] Hello.

17:05.900 --> 17:07.193
Mr. Ga!

17:07.277 --> 17:09.612
I'm back from Seoul safe and sound.

17:10.363 --> 17:13.408
-How was it?
-[gasps] It was super fun.

17:14.242 --> 17:15.285
Mr. Ga.

17:16.661 --> 17:18.872
Submit your field trip report
by the end of the week, okay?

17:19.622 --> 17:20.874
Okay.

17:27.338 --> 17:28.840
Time for attendance.

17:28.923 --> 17:29.924
[students] Okay.

17:31.593 --> 17:35.388
[students cheering, applauding]

17:35.472 --> 17:37.640
Okay, watch closely.

17:38.808 --> 17:40.518
Keep your feet shoulder-width apart

17:40.602 --> 17:41.936
and bend your knees slightly.

17:42.854 --> 17:44.230
Use both hands like so

17:44.898 --> 17:46.274
with one on the side.

17:46.357 --> 17:47.525
Now if you just shoot,

17:49.068 --> 17:50.153
it won't go in.

17:51.362 --> 17:52.947
You see the rectangle up there?

17:53.031 --> 17:55.408
You have to aim for that when you shoot…

17:57.577 --> 18:00.747
[students cheering, exclaiming]

18:02.832 --> 18:05.001
-…and you score.
-[students laughing]

18:05.084 --> 18:06.419
[chuckles] Let's do it.

18:07.712 --> 18:08.755
Ha-su.

18:16.638 --> 18:19.307
-There you go.
-[students cheering, exclaiming]

18:21.351 --> 18:22.852
-Way to go!
-Good job!

18:22.936 --> 18:24.145
That was so good.

18:26.898 --> 18:28.316
-[student 1 laughs]
-[student 2] She missed.

18:29.818 --> 18:31.611
Oh, my… [grunts]

18:31.694 --> 18:33.696
-[Gi-jeon] You're silly.
-I'm sorry. [chuckles]

18:33.780 --> 18:35.198
Go-ya.

18:36.574 --> 18:38.117
Don't mess around.

18:38.201 --> 18:40.286
[student laughs] This is crazy.

18:41.287 --> 18:42.539
Oh, wait. Wait.

18:42.622 --> 18:44.082
You have to use one hand, one hand.

18:44.833 --> 18:45.875
Like this.

18:46.501 --> 18:50.463
G-Go-ya's right wrist
is a little bit weak. It's fragile.

18:51.506 --> 18:53.842
So she sprains it often, that's all.

18:55.426 --> 18:56.511
Really?

18:58.972 --> 19:00.348
It's fine. I'll do it.

19:10.817 --> 19:12.193
[Gi-jeon] You can take a break.

19:13.236 --> 19:15.154
Did something happen between you two?

19:16.447 --> 19:18.408
No. Why?

19:19.242 --> 19:21.327
The whole vibe is different from usual.

19:22.203 --> 19:23.705
You aren't smiling.

19:24.289 --> 19:25.373
Go-ya's…

19:26.082 --> 19:28.126
just not feeling good. That's all.

19:28.209 --> 19:29.544
-[Jenny] Ah.
-[Eui-ju chuckles]

19:30.211 --> 19:31.754
[inhales sharply]

19:34.048 --> 19:36.384
Something definitely happened.

19:37.260 --> 19:39.721
MURIM GIRLS' HIGH SCHOOL

19:54.235 --> 19:55.445
[shutter clicking]

20:03.411 --> 20:04.704
Whoa.

20:07.874 --> 20:10.293
Crazy. Ji-a's actually rich.

20:10.376 --> 20:13.087
Some fancy-looking people
are escorting Ji-a in a car.

20:13.171 --> 20:14.213
[gasps]

20:14.297 --> 20:15.423
Whoa.

20:15.506 --> 20:19.636
Crazy. Crazy, crazy, crazy, crazy, crazy.

20:19.719 --> 20:21.888
-[urgent music playing]
-[panting]

20:29.896 --> 20:32.023
Oh! Mr. Ga! Mr. Ga, what do we do?

20:32.106 --> 20:34.233
It's Ji-a. I think those men
from yesterday got her.

20:34.317 --> 20:36.277
-What are you talking about?
-Look. Jenny saw them.

20:36.361 --> 20:39.948
Two men put Ji-a in this car and left.
What do we do? [panting]

20:40.031 --> 20:42.825
-Stay right here. I'll go find her.
-Okay. Wait, huh?

20:42.909 --> 20:44.285
Send me a picture of their car

20:44.369 --> 20:45.787
-and one of their business card.
-Okay.

20:49.916 --> 20:52.126
[groans] Oh, what do I do?

20:52.210 --> 20:54.587
What do I do? What do I do?
Think, Eui-ju, think.

20:55.546 --> 20:58.341
[gasps] Mr. Jung.
That's right. Mr. Jung. Mr. Jung.

20:58.424 --> 21:00.301
GOOD CONSCIENCE PAYDAY LOANS

21:12.855 --> 21:14.524
[thug 1] You picked it, right? Huh?

21:14.607 --> 21:15.858
WE'LL HELP LIKE YOU'RE FAMILY

21:15.942 --> 21:18.277
Run Course C three times
and that's a thousand bucks, got it?

21:18.361 --> 21:20.238
-Huh?
-Choi Ji-a.

21:21.114 --> 21:22.323
-Uh…
-Mr. Ga!

21:22.407 --> 21:24.325
No, no, no, no, no. Sit back down.

21:24.951 --> 21:27.453
-[whimpering]
-Holy cow.

21:28.371 --> 21:30.456
Didn't I tell you to stay away from her?

21:30.540 --> 21:32.333
The teacher came all the way here.

21:32.417 --> 21:33.543
[chuckles]

21:34.419 --> 21:36.004
[boss] And who is this?

21:37.463 --> 21:39.257
[thug 1] Oh, her homeroom teacher.

21:40.758 --> 21:42.635
Well, well.

21:42.719 --> 21:47.181
-A teacher's kindness is sky high, huh?
-[laughing]

21:47.265 --> 21:49.308
[thug 2]
Look, we're really sorry about this.

21:49.392 --> 21:51.936
But we did the math,
and it just didn't add up.

21:52.562 --> 21:53.771
Prices have gone up lately.

21:55.314 --> 21:56.941
You know what I mean, right?

21:57.025 --> 21:59.569
So we just had no other choice… [inhales]

21:59.652 --> 22:02.030
-…but to change our interest rates.
-[thug 1] Uh-huh.

22:02.113 --> 22:03.990
It used to be 20% a month,

22:04.073 --> 22:06.284
but we had to switch it to a weekly rate.

22:07.035 --> 22:10.663
While our dear Ji-a wasn't paying,
the interest rate just… [exclaims]

22:11.372 --> 22:12.373
…skyrocketed.

22:15.626 --> 22:18.463
So she's got about $1,700 left to pay.

22:18.546 --> 22:20.048
I already paid it all off.

22:20.131 --> 22:22.467
Mr. Ga, don't listen
to these people, please.

22:22.550 --> 22:23.718
Shut the hell up!

22:24.218 --> 22:25.219
Be quiet!

22:25.303 --> 22:27.096
Anyway, this is how it is, teacher.

22:27.180 --> 22:30.808
If Ji-a can't pay, we'll have no choice
but to have her work part-time

22:30.892 --> 22:34.020
at a nice place
with very pretty ladies, you know?

22:34.103 --> 22:35.313
-Wait, wait.
-Mr. Ga,

22:35.396 --> 22:37.315
don't give any more money to these people.

22:37.398 --> 22:38.941
I'm okay. Don't worry about me
and get out of here.

22:39.025 --> 22:40.526
[metal bats clanging]

22:43.321 --> 22:44.322
Do you have a contract?

22:45.990 --> 22:47.658
Show me the contract she signed.

22:47.742 --> 22:49.660
With those exact terms.
Go on, let's see it.

22:51.329 --> 22:52.413
Huh?

22:53.247 --> 22:55.166
Without it, what's all this based on, huh?

22:56.876 --> 22:58.586
[sighs]

22:59.462 --> 23:00.463
[clicks tongue]

23:00.546 --> 23:02.548
I've had a enough of you already.

23:03.966 --> 23:05.885
This place isn't a teacher's office, okay?

23:05.968 --> 23:08.012
-[grunts]
-[Ji-a gasps]

23:08.096 --> 23:09.097
Mr. Ga!

23:10.181 --> 23:11.682
[thug 1] Goodness!

23:11.766 --> 23:14.560
-[laughing]
-What's the matter with you? Huh?

23:17.146 --> 23:19.315
I guess you guys
haven't figured me out yet.

23:22.735 --> 23:25.029
-[thugs chuckling]
-[thug 1] Seriously?

23:26.614 --> 23:28.616
[intrepid music playing]

23:37.208 --> 23:39.210
[tires squeal]

23:40.711 --> 23:42.338
PAYDAY LOANS

23:48.511 --> 23:49.637
This must be it.

23:50.263 --> 23:52.515
Eui-ju, you better wait here.
We'll come back out with them.

23:53.099 --> 23:55.101
-But still, I…
-Wait there.

23:55.184 --> 23:56.185
Won't take long.

24:15.204 --> 24:16.831
[boss] You like jjajangmyeon that much?

24:16.914 --> 24:18.124
-[grunting]
-Yes, boss.

24:18.207 --> 24:20.251
[boss] Look at how much you like it, huh.
Is it good?

24:20.334 --> 24:21.711
[laughing]

24:27.383 --> 24:30.344
[Eui-ju] Mr. Ga! Are you okay?

24:30.428 --> 24:32.221
-[groans]
-Oh, no. Are you okay?

24:32.305 --> 24:33.556
Oh, I'm sorry.

24:33.639 --> 24:34.724
Oh, my. Mr. Ga.

24:35.933 --> 24:38.060
What are these beautiful angels
doing here?

24:38.811 --> 24:42.815
What brings such a divine presence
to this humble place?

24:43.357 --> 24:44.358
Did you do that

24:45.818 --> 24:46.861
to our boy right there?

24:47.528 --> 24:49.113
-[laughing]
-Yeah.

24:49.697 --> 24:51.032
[boss] Well, now.

24:51.115 --> 24:53.242
[Eui-ju] Oh, my goodness, Mr. Ga.

24:53.326 --> 24:55.119
[Eui-ju crying]

25:02.668 --> 25:04.337
[rock music playing]
